Description: Computes abstention-values (A-values), a decision-theoretic
    measure of the break-even welfare cost of collecting follow-up evidence
    instead of making an immediate policy decision. Supports vectorized point
    estimates, standard errors or exact two-sided normal p-values, and
    estimate-specific follow-up precision designs. Produces logarithmic
    A-value distributions and rank-comparison plots for prioritizing a fixed
    number of follow-up experiments.
